    "created_at": "2022-11-30T10:27:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-30T10:27:57Z",
    "body": "I think it would be best if we only exported navigable container document.\r\n\r\n- Other specs should generally not reference `CSP-derived sandboxing flags`; I see in https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/580 you are adding to a section that generally explains how HTML works, and for other items in that section, you use the `<a spec=html>un-exported term</a>` syntax to get access. That's what I'd recommend in this case.\r\n\r\n- The \"plugin\" term should go away completely, once someone makes time for it: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6003. Exporting the term so that others can create dependencies on it seems like a step backward.\r\n\r\nWDYT?",
